{
  "schema": "prova.verification-case/1",
  "title": "Node centralities of a signed weighted network",
  "description": "Strength, expected influence, closeness and betweenness of a ten-node signed network (the EBIC graphical lasso network of the bfi items, rounded to six decimals). Shortest paths run over 1 / |weight|. psychnets reports closeness and betweenness normalized as igraph does (normalized = TRUE); qgraph::centrality_auto() reports closeness as 1 / sum of distances and betweenness as a count of paths, so the qgraph script multiplies closeness by (p - 1) and divides betweenness by (p - 1)(p - 2) / 2, as psychnets' documentation states the relation.",
  "covers": [
    "net_centralities()"
  ],
